<Project Sdk="Dalamud.NET.Sdk/15.0.0">
 <PropertyGroup>
  <Version>0.1.0.16</Version><Author>CheesyChiz</Author><Name>XIVGear Prog</Name><InternalName>XivGearProg</InternalName>
  <Punchline>Sync equipped gear and saved gear sets with XIVGear Prog.</Punchline>
  <Description>Gear plans show owned, cached retainer and missing items, icons, target materia/relic stats and server-backed exchange prices. Rounded dark cards with turquoise accents and expandable saved plans per character. Exchange costs can be expanded and collapsed. Receive website builds immediately through a persistent account connection. Offline deliveries wait until you reconnect; Fetch sets is a manual retry. Preview equipment by slot and compare items, quality, materia and relic stats with equipped or saved game sets. Create a new game gear-set slot after reviewing. Does not equip items, meld materia or change relic stats. Connect your account using a revocable token. Sends your equipped gear and saved combat gear sets, including materia and relic stats, to xivgearprog.top. Syncs all unlocked combat job levels so the website recommends equippable gear and calculates at the correct level. Includes gear in bags and Armoury Chest. Includes currency and material balances. Prices are provided by the website server from Garland Tools. Use one token for multiple characters; select a character on the website. Retainer inventory snapshots update only after opening their inventories in game. Choose which jobs and individual gear sets to sync in /xgp. Open /xgp to connect; automatic checks run every 5 minutes and only changed data is sent. Use Sync now for an immediate update.</Description>
  <RepoUrl>https://github.com/CheesyChiz/DalamudPlugins/tree/main/src/XivGearProg</RepoUrl>
  <IconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CheesyChiz/DalamudPlugins/main/src/XivGearProg/assets/icon.png</IconUrl>
  <Tags>gear;gearsets;xivgear;sync</Tags><PackageLicenseExpression>AGPL-3.0-only</PackageLicenseExpression>
  <Nullable>enable</Nullable><ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings><AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
 </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
